    "https://schema.org/mainContentOfPage": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n\n\t\t\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t  \n          \n        \n      \n    \n\n    Thu Feb 11, 2027 • 7:30pm\n\n  \n          Music\n    \n          Rock\n      \n\n  Event length: 90 minutes\n\n      Admission $66.25\n    \n      Ticket prices include all taxes and fees.\n    \n  \n\n\n      \n  \n    Buy tickets\n  \n\n  \n  \n  \n  \n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t\t\n\t\n\t  \n    \n      \n                  Classic Albums Live \"Cars\"\n        \n                  \n            $66.25 || CLASSIC ALBUMS LIVE performs THE CARS : THE CARS\nthe cars started new wave\nthey weren’t quite punk\nand they sure as hell weren’t black sabbath or disco\nthey had a unique sound\nthe sound of change\nthis album was everywhere\nit was inside or on top of every stack of albums\nmany a car stereo was blasting let the good times roll in 1978\nan interesting note\nthat the same cat that produced queen\nproduced this album - roy thomas baker\nthat’s why the album sounds lush and nuanced\nlike many big bands\nthe cars’ secret was having two lead singers\nthe quirky rik ocasek and the cool benjamin orr\nbut the secret sauce was the guitar playing\nelliot easton was a master sound crafter\nhis virtuosity made the songs soar\nthe album will be fun to play\nbut i’m looking forward to the second set\nwhere we dig in to some great american songwriting\nand perform these works of art\nthe best way we know how\nnote for note - cut for cut\ncraig martin\nfounder, classic albums live\n          \n        \n              \n\n      \n  \n    Event Info\n\n          \n        Category: Music      \n    \n          \n        Genre: Rock      \n    \n          \n        Event Length: 90 minutes\n      \n    \n      \n  \n  \t\t\n\n\n      \n      Venue\n\n              Imperial Theatre\n      \n              12 King Square South, Saint John NB, E2L 5B8\n      \n              \n          \n            View on Google Maps\n          \n        \n          \n  \n  \n\n\n\n{\n    \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"Event\",\n    \"@id\": \"https://imperialtheatre.ca/event/classic-albums-live-cars/52201AGLBQNPLVLHRQSQHGRRPVTMJCMCR/#event-52201aglbqnplvlhrqsqhgrrpvtmjcmcr\",\n    \"name\": \"Classic Albums Live \\\"Cars\\\"\",\n    \"url\": \"https://imperialtheatre.ca/event/classic-albums-live-cars/52201AGLBQNPLVLHRQSQHGRRPVTMJCMCR/\",\n    \"eventAttendanceMode\": \"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\",\n    \"eventStatus\": \"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\",\n    \"location\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Place\",\n        \"name\": \"Imperial Theatre\",\n        \"sameAs\": [\n            \"http://kg.artsdata.ca/resource/K11-193\",\n            \"http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3527482\"\n        ],\n        \"address\": {\n            \"@type\": \"PostalAddress\",\n            \"streetAddress\": \"12 King Square South\",\n            \"addressLocality\": \"Saint John\",\n            \"postalCode\": \"E2L 5B8\",\n            \"addressRegion\": \"New Brunswick\",\n            \"addressCountry\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Country\",\n                \"name\": \"CA\"\n            }\n        }\n    },\n    \"organizer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"name\": \"Imperial Theatre\",\n        \"url\": \"https://imperialtheatre.ca/\"\n    },\n    \"description\": \"$66.25 || CLASSIC ALBUMS LIVE performs THE CARS : THE CARS the cars started new wave they weren’t quite punk and they sure as hell weren’t black sabbath or disco they had a unique sound the sound of change this album was everywhere it was inside or on top of every stack of albums many a car stereo was blasting let the good times roll in 1978 an interesting note that the same cat that produced queen produced this album - roy thomas baker that’s why the album sounds lush and nuanced like many big bands the cars’ secret was having two lead singers the quirky rik ocasek and the cool benjamin orr but the secret sauce was the guitar playing elliot easton was a master sound crafter his virtuosity made the songs soar the album will be fun to play but i’m looking forward to the second set where we dig in to some great american songwriting and perform these works of art the best way we know how note for note - cut for cut craig martin founder, classic albums live\",\n    \"image\": [\n        \"https://system.spektrix.com/imperialtheatrenewbrunswick/files/7947abc4-e05f-4b55-82d4-fd688a3a954c.jpg\"\n    ],\n    \"startDate\": \"2027-02-11T19:30:00-04:00\",\n    \"offers\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Offer\",\n        \"url\": \"https://imperialtheatrenewbrunswick.spektrix.com/imperialtheatrenewbrunswick/website/EventDetails.aspx?EventId=52201AGLBQNPLVLHRQSQHGRRPVTMJCMCR\",\n        \"availability\": \"https://schema.org/InStock\",\n        \"validFrom\": \"2027-02-11T19:30:00-04:00\"\n    },\n    \"performer\": {\n        \"@type\": \"Thing\",\n        \"additionalType\": [\n            \"http://dbpedia.org/ontology/Agent\",\n            \"http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent\"\n        ],\n        \"name\": \"Classic Albums Live \\\"Cars\\\"\"\n    }\n}\n\n\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\t\n\t\n\n\n\n\t"
